course: dictionary
lesson: 8797
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one you need. «The knife is sharp, so carry it point down.» Here sharp means having a thin edge or fine point that can cut.
explain: «She felt a sharp pain in her ankle.» You cannot cut with a pain, so sharp must mean sudden and strong. Always ask: which meaning fits these words? Then try it in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: «At three o'clock sharp» means exactly at three, and «sharp words» are unkind or angry. The phrase around sharp is the clue, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Sharp has several meanings, so the words around it show you which one is meant.
fact: A sharp object has a thin edge or fine point that can cut or pierce, like a knife or a needle.
fact: «Sharp» can also describe a turn or bend that changes direction quickly, or a clever person who notices things fast.
fact: «Look sharp» means hurry, «sharp as a tack» means very clever, and «at three o'clock sharp» means exactly on time.
fact: Keep sharp objects such as knives, scissors, glass and needles away from small children, carry them point down, and tell an adult about broken glass.
exercise: «The knife is sharp, so carry it point down.» What does sharp mean here? | Quick to notice | Very angry | *Having a thin edge that can cut | Hurrying
exercise: «He felt a sharp pain in his ankle.» What does sharp mean? | Exactly on time | Clever | Thin and fine | *Sudden and strong
exercise: «The car made a sharp turn to avoid the moose.» What does sharp suggest? | *Changed direction quickly | Very angry | Had a thin edge | Rang a bell
test: «Look sharp, or we will miss the bus!» What does look sharp mean? | *Hurry | Look at the sky | Stand very still | Sing loudly
test: «Jo is as sharp as a tack; she solved the puzzle first.» What does sharp as a tack mean? | Very tiny | *Very clever | Rusty and old | Very angry
exam: Ahmed says, «The meeting starts at three o'clock sharp.» What does sharp mean? | *Exactly on time | Quickly moving | Very angry | Made of metal, like a tack
